sentences.text:
The brief facts of the present case are that on 26.10.2005, at about 08:15p.m. the Food Inspectors Sh. Suniti Kumar Gupta and Field Assistant Sh. Satish Kumar Gaur ; under the supervision of Local Health Authority/SDM Sh. Vijay Dogra, reached at the premises of appellant/accused M/s Aggarwal Sweets, Opposite Sharadhanand College, Alipur, Delhi, where appellant/accused Pankaj Aggarwal,
vendor cum proprietor was found conducting business of various food articles which were lying stored/exposed for preparation of food article including Imli Ki Chatni for sale for human consumption ;
- that FI disclosed his identity and expressed his intention to purchase a sample of 'Imli Ki Chatni'
from the vendor which was lying there in a Tin container bearing no label declaration ;
- that thereafter as per the prescribed procedure under the PFA Act and Rules after giving notice to the vendor/appellant and offer towards the sale price of sample to which he agreed and accepted the sale consideration, sample was then lifted ;
- that each sample was separately packed, fastened, marked, sealed and necessary documents including Notice as per Form-VI in the presence of appellant/accused alongwith Panchnama etc was prepared at the spot ; the price of the sample commodity was paid to the vendor ;
- that thereafter one counterpart of sample was sent to Public Analyst (PA) in intact condition and other two counterparts were deposited with SDM/LHA ;
- that vide report dated 07.11.2005, the PA found the sample to be adulterated on the ground that it was coloured with synthetic colouring matter with "Sunset Yellow FEF" ; that the sample was misbranded because of complete violation of Rule 32 of PFA Rules - that upon receipt of report, SDM/LHA directed investigation which was carried out by Food Inspection and after completion of investigation sanction under Section 20 of the PFA Act was obtained from the Director PFA.
